                <pb facs="0252" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg132"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis transmits the information obtained from the Chinese minister at
                    Washington that the American stockholders of the Canton-Hankow Railway have
                    entered into an agreement to sell the concession and the railroad to the Chinese
                    Government for $6,750,000.)</p>
            </div>
